      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Our methodology utilizes a finely tuned variant of Cas9 nucleases to achieve targeted disruptions at three distinct genomic loci within the HEK293 cell line, specifically those encoding key metabolic enzymes integral to our experimental design. To enhance precision and excel at temporal and spatial gene expression control, our vectorization strategy employs ribonucleoprotein (RNP) complexes exclusive to the CRISPR-Cas9 system. Electroporation efficacy has been optimized for efficient transfection and minimized cellular stress, leveraging calibrated voltage parameters tailored for HEK293 cells. Post-transfection, we are committed to employing high-throughput next-generation sequencing (NGS) methodologies to ascertain the exactitude and efficiency of the induced genetic alterations, ensuring rigorous validation against our established genomic criteria.",
      "source": "target",
